\section{How to use}{

Build a query with the \verb{set_*()} functions and run a template by name:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{con |>
  set_area(area) |>
  set_grid(grid_type = "h3", resolution = 4) |>
  run_query(c("richness", "cell-sampling-bycell"))
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Templates ending in \code{-bycell} return one row per grid cell. Templates are stored per data product in \verb{sql/open-data/} and \verb{sql/speciesgrids/}; see \code{sql/README.md}.
}

\section{Sensitivity to sampling bias}{

Metrics tagged \emph{high} follow where and when people sampled and should be read next to the \emph{diagnostic} metrics (\code{cell-sampling}, \code{temporal-gaps}, ...). \emph{Moderate} metrics are partly corrected for effort; \emph{low} ones reflect data quality more than effort.
}

